# Per-user test configuration. Copy to `.env` (gitignored) and fill in your own
# values. `.env` is loaded by tests/conftest.py before tests run; never commit it.
# This keeps the test suite user-agnostic — no DB address lives in version control.

# A live Postgres storage URL enables the gated tune study-DB tests
# (`@pytest.mark.postgres`). Use a PASSWORD-LESS psycopg URL and let libpq read the
# password from ~/.pgpass or $PGPASSWORD (never put a password here or in argv).
# Unset → those tests are autoskipped.
#
#   PHENOTYPIC_TEST_PG_URL=postgresql+psycopg://USER@HOST:PORT/DBNAME
#
# How you stand up the server is your choice (institutional, cloud, or a
# user-space Slurm Postgres) — PhenoTypic only needs the URL. See the Phase-6
# distributed-tuning guide.
